WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.662
SOC 2 is an auditing and attestation framework developed by the American

00:00:04.662 --> 00:00:06.562
Institute of Certified Public Accountants,

00:00:06.562 --> 00:00:08.463
commonly known as the AICPA.

00:00:08.463 --> 00:00:13.025
It is used to evaluate whether an organization has designed and operates

00:00:13.025 --> 00:00:16.446
controls that support one or more Trust Services Criteria.

00:00:16.446 --> 00:00:19.867
Those criteria relate to security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality,

00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:20.627
and privacy.

00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:21.768
In everyday language,

00:00:21.768 --> 00:00:27.850
SOC 2 helps customers understand whether a service provider has practices in place to protect systems,

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:31.271
information, and commitments that matter to the customer relationship.

00:00:31.271 --> 00:00:35.833
SOC 2 is especially common for technology companies, SaaS providers, cloud services,

00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:36.973
managed service providers,

00:00:36.973 --> 00:00:42.675
and other organizations that handle customer data or operate important systems on behalf of others.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:46.857
A key point is that SOC 2 is not a certification.

00:00:46.857 --> 00:00:50.278
It is an independent attestation performed by qualified auditors.

00:00:50.278 --> 00:00:55.220
The resulting report describes the audit scope, the criteria included, the controls evaluated,

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.501
testing performed, and the auditor's opinion.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:01:02.062
Customers use SOC 2 reports during vendor reviews, procurement, risk assessments, renewals,

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.203
and security questionnaires.

00:01:03.203 --> 00:01:07.764
The report gives them a structured way to understand how the organization

00:01:07.764 --> 00:01:09.665
approaches trust and operational control.

00:01:09.665 --> 00:01:14.987
For employees, SOC 2 matters because the report is based on real operating practices.

00:01:14.987 --> 00:01:18.788
Policies, access controls, change records, monitoring activities, training, incident response,

00:01:18.788 --> 00:01:22.590
and evidence all come from normal work across the organization.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:26.011
This course provides an educational overview of SOC 2.

00:01:26.011 --> 00:01:30.192
It is not professional legal, accounting, regulatory, assurance, or compliance guidance.

00:01:30.192 --> 00:01:36.274
The goal is to help you understand the concepts and your role in supporting trustworthy operations.

00:01:36.274 --> 00:01:40.836
The most useful way to think about SOC 2 is as a

00:01:40.836 --> 00:01:42.737
trust conversation supported by evidence.

00:01:42.737 --> 00:01:47.679
The report helps an organization explain what it does, how controls are evaluated,

00:01:47.679 --> 00:01:51.860
and why customers can place confidence in the services being provided.
